Description: Emit "closed" when a popped-out AdwDialog is force-closed
 gtk-nocsd presents an AdwDialog in a window of its own. For a dialog in a
 window of its own, libadwaita's adw_dialog_force_close only closes the
 window: "closed" is not emitted and the dialog keeps its reference to the
 closed window. An embedded dialog emits "closed" when it is force-closed.
 .
 Epiphany keeps its preferences dialog until "closed" and force-closes it
 when preferences are opened from another window. It then still holds the
 dialog, which went with its window, and aborts on a GLib-GObject critical
 ("instance with invalid (NULL) class pointer").
 .
 In the adw_dialog_force_close hook, when the dialog is the content of its
 own window, close it as when its parent window is destroyed: "closed" is
 emitted once, even when can-close is FALSE, and can-close is restored
 afterwards. Other dialogs are force-closed as before.
Author: NeiroNext <mihail.rozshko@gmail.com>
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-17
---
--- a/Source/GTK-NoCSD.c
+++ b/Source/GTK-NoCSD.c
@@ -3541,6 +3541,15 @@ void adw_dialog_force_close(AdwDialog *D
 	GtkWindow *Window = (GtkWindow *) o_gtk_widget_get_ancestor(
 		(GtkWidget *) Dialog, GTKNoCSDGTKWindow);
 
+	// A dialog popped out into its own window is closed instead, so that
+	// closed is emitted as for an embedded one
+	if (Window != NULL &&
+		GTKNoCSDGTK4Content(GTKNoCSDWindowGetChild(Window)) ==
+		(GtkWidget *) Dialog) {
+		GTKNoCSDCloseDialog(Dialog);
+		return;
+	}
+
 	// Try to close
 	o_adw_dialog_force_close(Dialog);
 
